# Google Analytics & Search Console Credentials
# 
# To get this:
# 1. Go to Google Cloud Console: https://console.cloud.google.com
# 2. Create a new project or select existing
# 3. Enable these APIs:
#    - Google Analytics Data API
#    - Google Search Console API
# 4. Create a Service Account:
#    - Go to IAM & Admin > Service Accounts
#    - Click "Create Service Account"
#    - Give it a name (e.g., "analytics-portal")
#    - Click "Create and Continue"
#    - Skip the optional steps
# 5. Create a key:
#    - Click on the service account you just created
#    - Go to "Keys" tab
#    - Click "Add Key" > "Create new key"
#    - Choose JSON format
#    - Download the file
# 6. Add the service account to your GA4 properties:
#    - Go to Google Analytics Admin
#    - Select your property
#    - Go to "Property Access Management"
#    - Click the "+" button
#    - Add the service account email with "Viewer" role
# 7. Add the service account to Search Console:
#    - Go to Google Search Console
#    - Select your property
#    - Go to Settings > Users and permissions
#    - Add the service account email
# 8. Copy the ENTIRE contents of the downloaded JSON file and paste it below as a single line

GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS_JSON={"type":"service_account","project_id":"your-project-id","private_key_id":"...","private_key":"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n","client_email":"your-service-account@your-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com","client_id":"...","auth_uri":"https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth","token_uri":"https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token","auth_provider_x509_cert_url":"https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v1/certs","client_x509_cert_url":"..."}
